{"title":"Allen–Cahn","markdown":{"headingText":"Allen–Cahn","headingAttr":{"id":"sec-allen-cahn","classes":[],"keyvalue":[]},"containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n`apps/allen_cahn` — non-conserved phase-field dynamics, and the smallest\ncomplete application in the report.\n\n## Physical setting\n\nA two-phase system relaxing toward equilibrium by moving its interfaces.\nUnlike the Cahn–Hilliard model of @sec-cahn-hilliard, the order parameter here\nis **not** conserved: a grain can shrink and vanish. This is the standard model\nfor curvature-driven grain growth.\n\n## Governing equations\n\n$$\n\\partial_t \\phi \\;=\\; M\\nabla^2\\phi\n                 \\;-\\; \\frac{1}{\\varepsilon^2}\\big(\\phi^3 - \\phi\\big)\n                 \\;+\\; F ,\n$$ {#eq-ac-pde}\n\nwhere $\\varepsilon$ sets the interface width, the double-well term\n$\\phi^3-\\phi$ drives $\\phi$ toward $\\pm1$, and $F$ is an optional constant\ndriving force.\n\n## Conserved versus non-conserved\n\nThe contrast with @eq-ch-pde is the clearest illustration in this report of\nwhat the outer $\\nabla^2$ does. Cahn–Hilliard reads\n$\\partial_t c = M\\nabla^2(\\dots)$ and is conserved: in reciprocal space every\nterm carries the factor $u$, so the $\\mathbf{k}=0$ mode is annihilated and the\nmean cannot move.\n\n@eq-ac-pde has no outer Laplacian on the reaction term. Its $\\mathbf{k}=0$\ncomponent is $-\\varepsilon^{-2}(\\phi^3-\\phi) + F$, which is generally nonzero,\nso $\\langle\\phi\\rangle$ evolves freely. Physically: Cahn–Hilliard *redistributes*\na fixed amount of solute, Allen–Cahn *converts* one phase into another.\n\nThe consequence for verification is that the natural check is not conservation\nbut the growth of a favoured phase — which is what the test asserts.\n\n## Finite-difference formulation\n\nA second-order five-point Laplacian in $x$ and $y$ on a periodic slab, with\nseparated halo exchange, and explicit forward Euler:\n\n$$\n\\phi^{\\,n+1}_i \\;=\\; \\phi^{\\,n}_i \\;+\\; \\Delta t\\left[\n   M\\,(\\nabla^2_h\\phi^{\\,n})_i\n - \\frac{1}{\\varepsilon^2}\\big((\\phi^{\\,n}_i)^3 - \\phi^{\\,n}_i\\big)\n + F \\right].\n$$ {#eq-ac-update}\n\nTwo stability limits apply: the diffusive condition @eq-cfl, and a reaction\ncondition $\\Delta t \\lesssim \\varepsilon^2$ from the stiff double well. A sharp\ninterface is therefore expensive, which is the usual phase-field trade-off and\nthe reason $\\varepsilon$ is a numerical as well as a physical parameter.\n\n## Solution strategy\n\nExplicit Euler with separated halos, so the stencil evaluation and the halo\nexchange are distinct phases. Optional PNG snapshots of $\\phi$.\n\n## Verification\n\n* **Superlevel-set growth.** The area with $\\phi$ above a threshold grows by at\n  least a prescribed factor between $t=0$ and the end of the run — the\n  non-conserved counterpart to a conservation check.\n* **CPU–GPU parity.** Where CUDA/HIP twins are built.\n\n## Binaries and inputs\n\n`allen_cahn` (CPU), plus CUDA/HIP twins. Command-line driven; this application\ndoes not use the JSON session path.\n\n## Scalability\n\nNot measured.\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":""},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-